deals damage equal to its power to the other.)","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2018-10-05","toughness":null,"type_line":"Sorcery"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"If both target creatures are illegal targets by the time Undercity Uprising tries to resolve, the spell doesn’t resolve. No creatures deal damage or gain deathtouch.","oracle_id":"53e540b5-8338-4b21-a61a-c5b7fe652a6e","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If one of the two target creatures is an illegal target by the time Undercity Uprising tries to resolve, no creature deals or is dealt damage. Creatures you control still gain deathtouch.","oracle_id":"53e540b5-8338-4b21-a61a-c5b7fe652a6e","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Remember that a source with deathtouch has to deal damage, but not necessarily combat damage, to destroy another creature. As long as the fighting creature you control has power greater than 0 (and the damage isn’t prevented), the fighting creature you don’t control will be destroyed.","oracle_id":"53e540b5-8338-4b21-a61a-c5b7fe652a6e","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The first part of Undercity Uprising’s effect affects only creatures you control at the time it resolves. Creatures you begin to control later in the turn won’t gain deathtouch.","oracle_id":"53e540b5-8338-4b21-a61a-c5b7fe652a6e","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each player must discard three cards, even a player that (for some reason) didn’t actually draw three cards.","oracle_id":"af98156b-3064-4f16-940e-10039241f2b0","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"First the player whose turn it is draws three cards, then each other player in turn order does so. Then the active player randomly chooses the three cards they will discard, then each other player in turn order does so. Then all the cards are discarded at the same time.","oracle_id":"af98156b-3064-4f16-940e-10039241f2b0","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you have no other cards in hand, you'll have to discard one of the creature cards you return to your hand.","oracle_id":"cf75dbd8-b65a-48d9-b96b-4afb43f336d1","published_at":"2018-07-13","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You may cast Macabre Waltz targeting one or zero creature cards. You'll still discard a card, even if you target no creature cards.","oracle_id":"cf75dbd8-b65a-48d9-b96b-4afb43f336d1","published_at":"2018-07-13","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
